# /a34/backboardd.env: KEY=VALUE lines for backboardd's environment (copy this file to
# /a34/backboardd.env to use it; # starts a comment line). Another program the loader is inserted
# into has its own: /a34/SpringBoard.env, ... (there also A34GL_MODE=mesa|none|off). Read by a34gl-bbd before it execs the
# real backboardd, and by liba34gl-inject.dylib itself when the kernel inserts it (boot-arg
# a34inject=...): a variable the environment has already stays. Not read with boot-arg a34gl=0.
# The launchd job's EnvironmentVariables work as well (tools/root-add-job.py --env), except for
# DYLD_* variables, which launchd drops.

# The log of liba34gl and its loader. Without it: stderr, which the kernel copies into its log
# ("|backboardd| ..."). With it: that file only (backboardd runs as mobile: a file mobile may write).
#A34GL_LOG=/var/mobile/a34gl.log

# Switches of eagl.c, the words the kernel's boot-args may also carry (userland/a34gl/README.md):
#A34GL=glframes=1 glcopy=1

# Everything off (CoreAnimation's software renderer) without touching launchd.plist:
#A34GL_OFF=1

# Mesa and redwood-drm:
#PAN_MESA_DEBUG=sync
#REDWOOD_DRM_DEBUG=1
#EGL_LOG_LEVEL=debug

# redwood-drm: 0 sends every WAIT_BO and MADVISE to the kernel; 2 answers every MADVISE here
# (a measurement: userland/mesa/README.md). Default 1.
#REDWOOD_DRM_LOCAL=2
